      "slug": "kombu-dashi",
      "term": "Kombu dashi",
      "definition": "A light, clean Japanese stock made by cold-steeping dried kombu seaweed in water. It is the traditional broth for shabu-shabu as it adds umami without overpowering the delicate beef."
    },
    {
      "slug": "sesame-dipping-sauce",
      "term": "Sesame dipping sauce",
      "definition": "A creamy sauce made from sesame paste, soy sauce, mirin, and rice vinegar, served alongside shabu-shabu for dipping the cooked beef and vegetables."
    }
  ],
