  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Shabu-shabu uses a very lightly seasoned "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "kombu dashi",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "kombu-dashi"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " so the flavour of the beef comes through clearly. Each slice is cooked for just 5 to 10 seconds in the gently simmering broth before being dipped in "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "sesame dipping sauce",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "sesame-dipping-sauce"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " or ponzu. Serves 4."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ask your butcher to slice the beef paper-thin for shabu-shabu. Japanese supermarkets sell it pre-sliced. If slicing at home, freeze the beef for 45 minutes first to make it firm enough to cut thinly."
          }
        ]
      },
